# .percolate-ignore for the claude-klabauter-publish-repo-toplevel flat-mirror target
# (publish-targets.portable row `claude-klabauter-publish-repo-toplevel`).
#
# MECHANISM — a listed path is protected in BOTH directions (publish_sync.py
# `sync_flat_mirror`, both phases call the SAME `ignore.matches(rel_path)`):
#   Phase 1 (src->dst copy): not synced from this directory.
#   Phase 2 (dst delete-not-in-source): NOT deleted at the destination.
# Phase 2 is the dangerous half. It deletes every top-level destination file that this
# source directory does not contain, so a destination-native file that is not listed here
# is destroyed on the first publish. That is not hypothetical: the coordinator-claude
# sibling's own RESOLVED-2026-07-27 comment block records exactly this consequence being
# accepted for that mirror's CLAUDE.md when its protection line was removed.
#
# INVERSE, and equally load-bearing: a file we DO ship from this directory must NOT be
# listed. Listing it would make Phase 1 skip the copy, and the file would simply never
# reach the mirror. LICENSE, NOTICE.md, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md,
# PRIVACY.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, COMMERCIAL.md, CHANGELOG.md, AGENTS.md, pyproject.toml,
# conftest.py, and (as of the unscanned-published-noise fix) .gitignore are all shipped
# from here and are deliberately absent below.
#
# SCOPE — Phase 2 skips any destination entry that is not a file (`if not
# dst_file.is_file(): continue`), and the walk is `dst_dir.iterdir()`, non-recursive. The
# sweep therefore cannot reach a destination-native DIRECTORY or anything inside one:
# `.github/` and its contents are structurally out of reach and need no line here.
# Only top-level destination FILES need protecting.

# The .percolate-ignore file itself shouldn't appear in the publish repo root — it is a
# source-side control file, not OSS-facing content.
#
# Flat-mirror Phase 1 has NO dotfile skip -- unlike `sync_mirror`'s
# `_sync_mirror_top_level_files` helper, it checks only `ignore.matches(rel_path)`, never
# `rel_path.startswith(".")`. Without this line, this file would publish itself.
# `coordinator/dist/publish-repo-toplevel/.percolate-ignore` lists itself for the identical
# reason; this file follows that precedent.
.percolate-ignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Destination-native (publish-repo-owned) top-level files: authored in the mirror, never
# back-percolated here, and destroyed by the Phase-2 sweep unless named below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `.gitignore` used to be listed here (destination-native, hand-authored, never shipped
# from source) but no destination-native one was ever actually authored -- the published
# repo shipped with NO .gitignore at all, so anything that ran Python inside a fresh clone
# (a pytest run, a stray `python -m`) accumulated untracked `__pycache__/*.pyc` noise that
# then tripped `dispatch_end_of_run_unscanned_published_check` (499 false-positive findings
# on one real run, all `__pycache__/*.pyc`). Fixed by shipping a real `.gitignore` FROM
# this directory instead (see the sibling `.gitignore` file here) -- removed from the
# protection list below so Phase 1 actually copies it.

# The publish repo's Python venv pin -- per-publish-repo, not authored here.
.python-version

# Publish-side install-provenance sentinel, written at the END of a target sync (= source
# meta-repo HEAD) rather than authored in this directory. Protected so it is not churned
# -- deleted, then recreated -- on every publish.
version.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `state/` — PM ruling 2026-08-12: claude-klabauter's own working substrate (see
# claude-klabauter's CLAUDE.md, "`state/` is substrate") must never enter the
# claude-klabauter mirror. This directory has never staged a `state/` entry
# and is not expected to, but this line is a Phase-1 copy-time backstop for
# THIS row specifically: if `state/` were ever staged here (accidentally or
# by a future authoring mistake), branch-2 any-depth directory matching
# (ignore.py `is_ignored`) stops Phase 1 from copying it into the mirror.
#
# NOT a complete fix for this row's actual incident on its own — read the
# SCOPE note above first. This row's own Phase 2 (destination orphan sweep)
# is file-only and non-recursive (`dst_dir.iterdir()`, `if not
# dst_file.is_file(): continue`), so it structurally cannot reach a
# directory at the destination either way; a `state/` directory already
# present in the mirror by some OTHER path (e.g. a runtime writer, not this
# row) is outside this file's reach by construction, same as `.github/`
# above. That incident's actual root cause is the runtime writer
# (`coordinator_core/state_root.py`), fixed separately, not this publish
# row. This line closes this row's own copy-time contribution path, which
# is the only lever a `.percolate-ignore` file gives it.
state/
